  {
    "timestamp": "2026-04-08T23:59:23.328130",
    "event_type": "historical_post",
    "content": {
      "post_content": "Your code working means nothing.\nIt\u2019s what happens when it breaks that defines you.\n\nI used to measure progress by finished courses and clean PRs.\nThen production taught me about retries, partial failures, silent latency creep, and engineering judgment.\n\nIn this week\u2019s No Reset Required, I wrote about why transitions (BI \u2192 DE \u2192 SDE) don\u2019t happen when your code works.\nThey happen when you start thinking in failure modes.\n\nIf you\u2019re studying 2 hrs a day and trying to level up without resetting your career - this shift changes everything.\n\u2026more",
      "hashtags": [],
      "length": 547,
      "engagement": {
        "likes": "0",
