    "profile_id": "haymang",
    "id": "bae9b982-4215-4308-92c1-74cbfbb5766b"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "2026-04-08T23:59:23.333981",
    "event_type": "historical_post",
    "content": {
      "post_content": "Most people think moving from Data Engineer to Software Engineer means starting over.\n\n-> New identity.\n-> New stack.\n-> New fundamentals.\nThat wasn\u2019t my experience.\n\nI didn\u2019t reset.\nI expanded.\n\n# The distributed systems intuition I built tuning Spark jobs\u2026\n# The production ownership from broken pipelines at 2 AM\u2026\n# The cost discipline from writing design docs\u2026\nAll of it transferred.\n\nWhat changed wasn\u2019t my field.\nIt was my scope.\n\nIn Issue #9 of No Reset Required, I write about:\n\u2022 What actually transfers from data engineering to backend\n\u2022 What I had to learn from scratch\n\u2022 What didn\u2019t change\n\u2022 And why most \u201ccareer switches\u201d are really scope expansions\n\nIf you\u2019re feeling boxed into your current title, this one is for you.\nIssue #9 is live.\n\u2026more",
      "hashtags": [],
      "length": 756,
      "engagement": {
        "likes": "0",
        "comments": "0",
        "shares": "0"
      },
      "original_timestamp": ""
    },
    "metrics": {
      "likes": 0,
