  {
    "timestamp": "2026-04-08T23:59:23.397672",
    "event_type": "historical_post",
    "content": {
      "post_content": "I spent years studying after work.\n\n\nSet up Hadoop on my laptop.\nLearned HDFS, Hive, Spark. Took notes like a school kid. All this while I was working full time at Infosys. And still felt stuck for a long time.\n\nThis week\u2019s issue of No Reset Required is about the phase nobody talks about \u2014 the slow middle, where you\u2019re doing the right things but progress feels invisible.\n\nIf you\u2019re navigating a career transition and wondering why effort isn\u2019t translating yet, this one\u2019s for you.\n\u2026more",
