  {
    "timestamp": "2026-04-08T23:59:23.409317",
    "event_type": "historical_post",
    "content": {
      "post_content": "I didn\u2019t come from a CS degree or a top-tier college. Most people thought that would define my career \u2014 but it barely mattered.\n\nMy first job? Infosys training in Mysore. Java felt impossible. SQL was a struggle. I spent nights learning, asking \u201csilly\u201d questions, and practicing more than anyone else.\n\nFast forward: today I\u2019m a Senior Software Developer at Amazon, building backend systems and GenAI applications. And that first struggle taught me a lesson I wish everyone starting out knew:\n\nYour starting point matters far less than how quickly you turn exposure into leverage.\n\nI just published the first issue of my newsletter, No Reset Required, where I share my career journey from BI \u2192 Data Engineering \u2192 Software Engineering, the trade-offs, surprises, and decisions that made it all possible.\n\nRead the full article. Link in the comments section.\n\u2026more",
      "hashtags": [],
      "length": 862,
      "engagement": {
        "likes": "0",
        "comments": "1",
        "shares": "0"
      },
      "original_timestamp": ""
    },
    "metrics": {
      "likes": 0,
