  {
    "timestamp": "2026-04-08T23:59:23.458800",
    "event_type": "historical_post",
    "content": {
      "post_content": "Confession: I struggle to read. But I\u2019m still trying to build the habit.\n\nI love learning.\nI\u2019ve constantly upskilled \u2014 \nBI \u2192 Data Engineer \u2192 Software Developer.\n\nBut reading?\nThat\u2019s been my hardest habit to build.\n\nBooks.\nLong articles.\nEven LinkedIn posts sometimes.\n\nI struggle to stay consistent.\n\nSo I found workarounds: \n\u2022 learning by building first, reading later\n\u2022 breaking concepts by debugging real problems\n\u2022 teaching what I\u2019ve learned to reinforce it\n\u2022 consuming ideas in small, practical chunks\n\nThose workarounds helped me grow without being blocked.\n\nBut here\u2019s the truth:\nReading still helps. A lot.\n\nIt deepens thinking.\nIt connects dots faster.\nIt exposes you to ideas you wouldn\u2019t hit while \u201cjust doing.\u201d\n\nSo while reading isn\u2019t my natural strength,\nit\u2019s a habit I\u2019m consciously trying to build \u2014 slowly, intentionally.\n\nNot perfect.\nNot daily streaks.\nJust progress.\n\n. . . .\n\nWhat\u2019s a habit you know helps \u2014 but still struggle to stay consistent with?\n\nLet\u2019s be honest \ud83d\udc47\n\u2026more",
