  {
    "timestamp": "2026-04-08T23:59:23.478919",
    "event_type": "historical_post",
    "content": {
      "post_content": "Most \u201cAI Pipelines\u201d Are Just Rebranded Data Pipelines\n\nEveryone says they\u2019re building AI pipelines now.\n\nBut under the hood, most of them are still:\n\u2022 data ingestion\n\u2022 transformation\n\u2022 storage\n\u2022 serving\n\nThe only real differences:\n\u2022 embeddings instead of aggregates\n\u2022 prompts instead of SQL\n\u2022 latency suddenly matters a lot\n\nAI didn\u2019t replace data engineering.\nIt exposed weak data engineering.\n\nIf your data isn\u2019t:\n\u2022 fresh\n\u2022 reliable\n\u2022 explainable\n\nno model will save you.\n\nThe uncomfortable truth:\nMost GenAI failures are data + system failures, not model failures.\n\nAI systems are just data systems with much tighter SLAs.\n\n. . . .\n\nIf you\u2019re building GenAI in production,\nwhat broke first for you \u2014 data quality, latency, or cost?\n\u2026more",
