  {
    "timestamp": "2026-04-08T23:59:23.490815",
    "event_type": "historical_post",
    "content": {
      "post_content": "80% of \u201cAI engineering\u201d today is just glue code wrapped in hype\n\n\nEveryone is talking about agents, LLM apps, retrieval, orchestration\u2026\nbut nobody is talking about the real engineering challenges behind them.\n\nHere\u2019s what actually matters if you want to build real AI systems:\n\n1\ufe0f\u20e3 Latency budgets\nUsers won\u2019t wait 6 seconds for a response.\nReasoning is cool. Slowness is not.\n\n2\ufe0f\u20e3 Context discipline\nDumping 200 pages into an LLM isn\u2019t \u201csmart.\u201d\nOptimized retrieval beats brute force every time.\n\n3\ufe0f\u20e3 Determinism boundaries\nBusiness logic \u2192 deterministic\nReasoning logic \u2192 probabilistic\nMix them carefully, or the system becomes unpredictable.\n\n4\ufe0f\u20e3 Monitoring & evaluation\nYou can\u2019t \u201ctest\u201d an AI system, you evaluate it.\nAnd 95% of teams don\u2019t even do that.\n\n\nEveryone wants to build AI products.\nBut the winners will be the ones who apply engineering rigor, not just clever prompts.\n\n\nWhat is that one thing you realized while building AI products that you think you could\u2019ve done better for the product?\n\u2026more",
      "hashtags": [],
      "length": 1011,
      "engagement": {
        "likes": "3",
        "comments": "0",
        "shares": "0"
      },
