  },
  {
    "timestamp": "2026-04-08T23:59:23.509863",
    "event_type": "historical_post",
    "content": {
      "post_content": "Stop trying to \u201clook senior.\u201d Start doing what senior engineers actually do.\n\n\n\nMost engineers chase the signals of seniority:\nFancy architecture diagrams.\nPerfect code reviews.\nBig technical words.\n\nBut here\u2019s the truth:\nYou don\u2019t grow by looking senior. You grow by thinking senior.\n\nHere\u2019s what that actually looks like:\n\n- Model systems, not functions\nAnyone can write code.\nSeniors understand how that code behaves inside a moving system.\n\n- Own problems, not tickets\nYou\u2019re not closing Jira tasks, you\u2019re reducing business friction.\n\n- Optimize for simplicity\nThe more experience you gain, the more allergic you become to complexity.\n\n- Document decisions, not just code\nA good doc saves you from a bad week.\n\n- Ask better questions\nNot \u201cWhat\u2019s the fix?\u201d\nBut \u201cWhy does this break? And how can we prevent it from breaking again?\u201d\n\nYour title changes after your thinking does.\nNot the other way around.\n\n\nWhat\u2019s one mindset shift that helped you level up as an engineer?\n\nDrop it in the comments - someone reading this might need it today.\n\u2026more",
      "hashtags": [],
      "length": 1049,
      "engagement": {
        "likes": "12",
        "comments": "4",
        "shares": "0"
      },
