  },
  {
    "timestamp": "2026-04-08T23:59:23.516447",
    "event_type": "historical_post",
    "content": {
      "post_content": "Career myth:\n\n\u201cYou need a perfect plan to switch tracks.\u201d\n\nReality:\nYou need momentum, curiosity, and a willingness to look stupid for a while.\n\nI\u2019ve officially transitioned from Senior Data Engineer \u2192 Senior Software Engineer.\n\nThis is: \nNot a \u201cperfect path.\u201d\nNot a \u201c10-step guide.\u201d\n\nJust a reminder:\nYou\u2019re allowed to reinvent yourself \u2014 even after becoming good at something.\n\nThe transition wasn\u2019t a leap. It was a series of tiny upgrades:\n- Getting obsessed with the why, not just the how\n- Saying \u201cyes\u201d to projects that scared me\n- Asking stupid questions (early) so I could avoid stupid mistakes (late)\n- Building things I wasn\u2019t \u201csupposed\u201d to build\n- Pairing with engineers smarter than me\n- Learning systems end-to-end\n- Shipping messy v1s instead of waiting for perfect v10s\n\n\nIf you\u2019re sitting on a transition you\u2019ve been postponing\u2026 my DMs are open.\nTake the next uncomfortable step.\n\nYour future self is already thanking you.\n\u2026more",
      "hashtags": [],
      "length": 944,
      "engagement": {
        "likes": "4",
        "comments": "1",
        "shares": "0"
