  },
  {
    "timestamp": "2026-04-08T23:59:23.639109",
    "event_type": "historical_post",
    "content": {
      "post_content": "How I carve out 2 hours/day for learning while working full-time at Amazon (Part 2)\n\nHere\u2019s something important:\nI\u2019m not saying you should pour your entire weekend into learning.\nFamily time, leisure, and rest are equally important.\n\nWhat I do recommend is balance:\n-> Weekdays: ~2 focused hours/day (often split into 2 sessions)\n-> Weekends: 2 hours total \u2014 just enough to keep momentum without sacrificing downtime\n\nThis small but consistent rhythm compounds massively.\nOver a year, that\u2019s ~700 hours of intentional learning.\nEnough to master a new skill, earn a certification, or even publish your own side projects.\n\nThe real secret?\nConsistency beats intensity.\nAnd protecting both growth and life outside work keeps you sustainable long term. It helps you from getting worn out. \n\nHow do you balance learning with your personal commitments?\n\u2026more",
