  },
  {
    "timestamp": "2026-04-08T23:59:23.652544",
    "event_type": "historical_post",
    "content": {
      "post_content": "\ud83e\udd16 AI won\u2019t replace your job. But it will replace parts of it.\n\nI\u2019ve noticed a big shift in how I use AI tools daily \u2014 not for flashy tasks, but for the \u201cmicro-frictions\u201d that slow me down.\n\nHere are 3 ways AI saves me hours each week:\n\n1\ufe0f\u20e3 Summarizing noise \u2192 signal.\nInstead of reading 20 pages of docs, I ask AI to give me the 5 key takeaways.\n\n2\ufe0f\u20e3 Idea scaffolding.\nWhen I\u2019m stuck on a blank page, I let AI throw the first 3\u20134 outlines at me. I don\u2019t copy them \u2014 but they break the block.\n\n3\ufe0f\u20e3 Code snippets & boilerplate.\nSimple scripts or regex patterns that used to take 30 minutes now take 3.\n\nEven tech giants like Amazon are pushing engineers to adopt PDD (Prompt-Driven Development) \u2014 especially for boilerplate code \u2014 to boost productivity and reduce time-to-delivery.\n\nThe insight: AI isn\u2019t a replacement. It\u2019s a force multiplier. The winners won\u2019t be the ones who \u201cavoid\u201d AI \u2014 but those who learn to weave it into their daily workflow.\n\n\ud83d\udc49 What\u2019s one task you wish AI could take off your plate today?\n\u2026more",
