  {
    "timestamp": "2026-04-08T23:59:23.719704",
    "event_type": "historical_post",
    "content": {
      "post_content": "Sometimes it\u2019s not the big job title.\nIt\u2019s that one project where everything clicked.\n\n\n\n\nBack when I was working at a mobility startup, we were building shuttle services for office commuters\u2014think pre-booked rides, fixed stops, and real-time seat tracking.\n\nIt sounded simple. But under the hood, everything depended on GPS data.\n \u2022 Drivers had mobile devices streaming location every few seconds\n \u2022 Every trip needed to be tracked live\n \u2022 Delays or missing data broke the experience for riders and ops teams\n\nThe Problem?\nWe were manually ingesting and validating GPS logs from hundreds of shuttles\u2014every single day.\nDelays, schema mismatches, missing timestamps\u2014it was chaos.\nAnd we were spending 10\u201312 hours just fixing things so analytics and routing systems wouldn\u2019t fail.\n\nNo one had time to fix the root cause.\nSo I took it up.\n\n\u2e3b\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\n\nWhat I built:\n\nAn automated GPS ingestion and validation pipeline that replaced manual work with a robust, scalable system:\n\n1. Real-time ingestion using AWS S3 + Lambda\n \u2022 Devices uploaded trip logs to a secure S3 bucket\n \u2022 A Lambda function triggered on file upload, parsed the data, and sent metadata for downstream processing\n\n2. Validation service (Python + FastAPI)\n \u2022 Checked for gaps in timestamp sequences\n \u2022 Verified route IDs, geofences, and malformed lat/lng pairs\n \u2022 Logged validation errors in DynamoDB for traceability\n\n3. Processed data pushed to Redshift via Spark jobs\n \u2022 Batched clean data for downstream analytics\n \u2022 Scheduled every 30 minutes using Airflow\n\n4. Alerting & Monitoring (CloudWatch + Slack Webhooks)\n \u2022 Any invalid data or failed processing triggered an alert\n \u2022 Summary reports were sent to ops + tech every morning\n\n\u2e3b\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014-\n\nThe Impact:\n \u2022 Cut pipeline processing time from 10+ hours to 25 minutes\n \u2022 Reduced manual effort by 90%\n \u2022 Made live trip analytics and routing much more reliable\n \u2022 Increased trust between tech and ops\u2014this system just worked\n\n\u2e3b\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014-\n\nCareer-wise?\nThis was the project that changed everything. I wasn\u2019t just a \u201cdata guy\u201d anymore. I was the one who solved a pain point that everyone had accepted as normal.\n\n\n\nWhat\u2019s your breakout project?\nOr what\u2019s the problem at your job no one wants to touch\u2014but needs solving?\n\u2026more",
