    "event_type": "historical_post",
    "content": {
      "post_content": "\ud83d\udea8 \"Fine-tuning your LLM? You might be wasting time and money.\" \ud83d\udea8\nWhen building GenAI apps, many developers instinctively jump to fine-tuning\u2014but Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) is a smarter, faster, and often better solution.\nIn my latest blog, I break down:\n\ud83d\udc49 What RAG is and how it works\n\ud83d\udc49 When to use RAG vs. fine-tuning\n\ud83d\udc49 Real-world examples and code snippets for building GenAI apps\n\nIt\u2019s time to stop over-engineering and start building smarter. Curious about how RAG can revolutionize your projects? Let\u2019s discuss!\n\n\nhashtag\n#MachineLearning \nhashtag\n#ArtificialIntelligence \nhashtag\n#SoftwareDevelopment \nhashtag\n#LargeLanguageModels\n\u2026more",
